['Subject: re : current var issues  
here are the current issues related to var and credit models :
1 . factor loadings ( fl ) for all " primary " commodities :
- the code is tested ;
- factors loadings have been calculated for every primary curve and examined
closely by research ;
- using different number of maturities for fl calculations ( it ) ;
- selecting " good " curves , setting mappings for the others ( rac ) ;
2 . reviewing power var model :
- implementing term structure of correlations ( preliminary research is in
progress by research , to be implemented by it ) ;
- implementing caps in var model ( it ) ;
- jumps for intramonth prices ( re - examine prices behavior , research ) ;
3 . historical ff vols ( research , rac ) ;
4 . interest rate and fx :
- preliminary research is completed ( research ) ;
- implementation in risktrack ( it ) ;
5 . credit model :
- resolving the problem of identical runs giving different results ( it with
research ' s help ) ;
6 . mg metals var model :
- merging with risktrack ( rac , it , research ) ;
- refining the model ( research ) ;
7 . var calculations for uk curves :
- merging with risktrack , elimination spreadsheets ( rac , it , research ) ;
- looking closely at var calculations for each commodity ;
8 . merchant portfolio var :
- unification with equity var model ;
9 . fat tails modeling ( research ) ;
let me know what i missed .
thank you ,
tanya .']

["Subject: fw : pg & e withdrawal of open season application  
fyi - - pg & e has withdrawn their open season application . mark and i will continue to monitor pg & e ' s filings for the gas accord ii filing which many had expected would be filed by this point in time . gh
- - - - - original message - - - - -
from : mbaldwin @ igservice . com @ enron [ mailto : imceanotes - mbaldwin + 40 igservice + 2 ecom + 40 enron @ enron . com ]
sent : friday , august 17 , 2001 6 : 00 pm
to : glen hass
subject : fw : pg & e withdrawal of open season application
glen ,
in case you have not seen this pg & e motion . pg & e is calling it quits on its
backbone open season application . it is clear that pg & e can not maintain
its plan roll out for this open season and therefore one of the primary
reasons to do this at all ( keeping pace with ruby and sonoran pipelines ) has
been made impossible . next , there was a growing consensus that market
participants required more information concerning backbone rates and
operational structure . these items would be included in the long awaited gas
accord ii filing . pg & e has to file its gas accord ii , then i would expect a
likely re application of an open season . no definite word on when the g ii
will be filed . mark , igs .
- - - - - original message - - - - -
